evidence_source:
In modbus_reply():
  offset = ctx->backend->header_length;
  function = req[offset];
  address = (req[offset + 1] << 8) + req[offset + 2];
For server receive, _modbus_receive_msg(MSG_INDICATION) uses compute_meta_length_after_function(); for 0x11 (and any code not matched), it returns 0, so only header+1 (8 bytes) are read before returning to the caller. No req_length check is performed in modbus_reply() before reading offset+1 and offset+2.
